WEBVTT

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:12.610
Isn't that...

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:22.290
Hey.

00:00:22.290 --> 00:00:24.710
You come here pretty often, don't you?

00:00:24.710 --> 00:00:26.250
Are you wishing for something?

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:27.190
What's your name?

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:30.990
Uh... I'm Rio.

00:00:30.990 --> 00:00:34.790
I heard this shrine can cure diseases.

00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:39.100
My mom has a weird disease.

00:00:39.410 --> 00:00:41.000
A weird disease?

00:00:41.560 --> 00:00:44.980
I'm Dr. Ramune. I'm actually 
a bit of a weird doctor myself.

00:00:46.730 --> 00:00:48.470
A doctor?

00:00:48.470 --> 00:00:52.180
That's right. As you can see, I'm 
a super-ultra-great doctor who—

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:53.860
<b>Mysterious Disease Specialist</b>

00:00:52.180 --> 00:00:53.850
Doctor, phone for you.

00:00:54.630 --> 00:00:56.890
I'll listen to what you have to say.

00:00:56.890 --> 00:00:59.210
Kuro, take care of this kid.

00:00:59.690 --> 00:01:01.870
All right. Come in, please.

00:01:02.380 --> 00:01:05.620
Hello, Dr. Ramune here.

00:01:06.570 --> 00:01:09.330
I see, I see. A patient 
with a mysterious illness.

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:10.850
Thanks as always.

00:01:11.470 --> 00:01:13.250
What? Her ears?

00:01:13.250 --> 00:01:16.140
Wait, you're not an otorhinolaryngologist.

00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:21.050
I see.

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:23.560
Excuse me.

00:01:24.830 --> 00:01:27.450
Looks like she just arrived.

00:01:27.450 --> 00:01:28.110
Bye.

00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:34.280
I was referred here.

00:01:34.610 --> 00:01:36.070
Mom?

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:12.370
<b>Dr. Ramune
Mysterious Disease Specialist</b>

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:17.960
<b>Episode 5 "Pot Sticker Ears – Part One"</b>

00:03:15.930 --> 00:03:18.340
Your ears turned into pot stickers?

00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:23.570
Yes. I can't pull them off, and 
can't pierce them with a needle.

00:03:24.860 --> 00:03:26.100
Thanks.

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:27.010
Thank you.

00:03:38.450 --> 00:03:39.820
Here you go.

00:03:43.740 --> 00:03:46.080
Thank you.

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:49.320
Here, Yuu. Are you okay with hot drinks?

00:03:49.730 --> 00:03:51.570
Yeah, I'm fine.

00:03:51.570 --> 00:03:52.690
Yuu?

00:03:52.690 --> 00:03:54.570
That's my brother's name.

00:03:56.830 --> 00:03:59.740
So, how long have you had those ears?

00:03:59.740 --> 00:04:02.210
Since October of last year.

00:04:02.210 --> 00:04:05.640
Since then, I'm occasionally 
unable to hear people's voices.

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:09.240
I believe it's because my 
ears turned into these.

00:04:09.240 --> 00:04:10.390
Hmm.

00:04:10.390 --> 00:04:15.560
By the way, mysterious diseases 
are generally caused by stress.

00:04:16.150 --> 00:04:19.270
Did something happen last October?

00:04:28.330 --> 00:04:30.550
No, nothing.

00:04:33.170 --> 00:04:38.670
But since then, my head sometimes 
feels foggy and my memory is hazy.

00:04:38.670 --> 00:04:41.500
I'm currently visiting a 
psychiatrist for counseling.

00:04:44.440 --> 00:04:45.960
That was close.

00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:49.880
Yuu, are you okay?!

00:04:49.880 --> 00:04:50.960
Did you get any on you?!

00:04:52.170 --> 00:04:53.730
I'm fine.

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:58.560
Good. You nearly got burned again.

00:04:58.560 --> 00:04:59.480
Excuse me—

00:05:16.380 --> 00:05:20.210
I'm sorry. I didn't catch that.

00:05:22.410 --> 00:05:23.360
Excuse me—

00:05:23.980 --> 00:05:29.140
I see. Those pot stickers 
sometimes envelope voices.

00:05:29.140 --> 00:05:32.760
That shouldn't interfere with
 your private life, though.

00:05:33.010 --> 00:05:34.930
That's not true!

00:05:34.930 --> 00:05:38.560
For some reason, I can't 
hear everything Rio says.

00:05:38.560 --> 00:05:40.720
I can't hold a proper conversation with him.

00:05:41.130 --> 00:05:43.110
Can't you do something?

00:05:44.190 --> 00:05:46.520
How should I explain this?

00:05:47.130 --> 00:05:50.640
From the looks of it, your ear 
holes aren't completely blocked.

00:05:50.640 --> 00:05:53.050
And it's only parts of certain 
voices that you can't hear.

00:05:53.720 --> 00:05:57.750
In other words, they're differentiating 
between voices you can hear normally

00:05:57.750 --> 00:06:00.380
and those that get enveloped 
by the pot stickers.

00:06:00.380 --> 00:06:03.300
Rio's voice is the latter.

00:06:03.300 --> 00:06:07.180
Once your actual ears hear the 
voices you were supposed to hear

00:06:07.180 --> 00:06:11.090
but were blocked by the pot 
stickers, they'll come off.

00:06:11.090 --> 00:06:14.300
You'll be able to hear Rio's voice again.

00:06:14.920 --> 00:06:18.060
But this isn't a matter of logic. 
It's a matter of the heart.

00:06:18.460 --> 00:06:21.200
Why do the pot stickers envelope voices?

00:06:21.560 --> 00:06:24.570
You should carefully think 
on the reason again.

00:06:25.300 --> 00:06:27.480
Anyway, we'll see how things go.

00:06:27.480 --> 00:06:29.650
Come back once you've 
figured something out.

00:06:29.650 --> 00:06:31.360
Very well.

00:06:31.840 --> 00:06:34.570
Excuse me. Where's your restroom?

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:36.210
Over there.

00:06:36.700 --> 00:06:38.260
Yuu, do you need to go, too?

00:06:38.260 --> 00:06:39.030
Yeah.

00:06:41.430 --> 00:06:43.440
Can I take this?

00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:46.800
I hate this.

00:06:47.580 --> 00:06:51.050
No matter who she asks, it's always, 
"Come back another time."

00:06:52.090 --> 00:06:57.200
This shrine cures diseases, 
and you're a doctor, right?

00:06:57.980 --> 00:07:00.760
Please cure my mom.

00:07:01.280 --> 00:07:03.340
I'll do anything!

00:07:10.140 --> 00:07:12.150
There is a treatment method 
that's most effective.

00:07:12.150 --> 00:07:15.040
I didn't recommend it 
because it involves you.

00:07:16.300 --> 00:07:19.130
But you said you'd do anything, right?

00:07:22.550 --> 00:07:23.360
Yeah.

00:07:24.090 --> 00:07:27.260
Doctor, he's only a child.

00:07:27.260 --> 00:07:29.540
Just to be sure,

00:07:29.950 --> 00:07:32.410
do you have a dick?

00:07:32.410 --> 00:07:33.680
<i>What?!</i>

00:07:34.170 --> 00:07:35.340
Yes!

00:07:37.560 --> 00:07:38.620
All right, Kuro.

00:07:38.620 --> 00:07:41.060
Blue shelf, fifth row. 
Second from the right.

00:07:41.060 --> 00:07:42.600
What? Oh, right.

00:07:46.560 --> 00:07:47.720
What is this?

00:07:48.240 --> 00:07:52.280
The Pearl of Night Voices. It's mysterious 
item that's a teensy bit odd.

00:07:53.090 --> 00:07:59.320
You said you'd cure your mom, 
so naturally, you'll pay the price.

00:08:00.700 --> 00:08:03.320
The price is your voice.

00:08:04.030 --> 00:08:06.860
Whether or not she's cured is up to you.

00:08:13.140 --> 00:08:17.950
Are you sure you should've given him that 
mysterious item without knowing the cause?

00:08:18.340 --> 00:08:19.860
You think I don't know?

00:08:20.170 --> 00:08:23.250
Kuro, you're not that dumb.

00:08:23.250 --> 00:08:26.100
You have some idea what the cause is.

00:08:27.820 --> 00:08:33.520
In fact, she's the only one 
who doesn't understand.

00:08:36.610 --> 00:08:37.480
Excuse me.

00:08:39.190 --> 00:08:40.050
Yuu-kun's—

00:08:46.620 --> 00:08:47.290
I said—

00:08:47.290 --> 00:08:50.380
Don't! Please stop coming here!

00:08:50.380 --> 00:08:52.530
Mom, let's go inside the house.

00:08:52.530 --> 00:08:53.270
What?

00:08:52.530 --> 00:08:53.950
Um, I...

00:08:58.390 --> 00:08:59.590
Welcome back.

00:08:59.590 --> 00:09:02.020
What's wrong? Did something happen?

00:09:02.440 --> 00:09:06.630
Someone spoke to me in 
front of the house again.

00:09:08.910 --> 00:09:13.110
Since I can't hear his voice, 
I don't know what he's saying,

00:09:13.110 --> 00:09:16.270
but he keeps coming here.

00:09:16.270 --> 00:09:18.190
Probably a solicitor.

00:09:18.190 --> 00:09:19.550
Don't let him bother you.

00:09:23.390 --> 00:09:25.100
I see.

00:09:25.680 --> 00:09:28.580
Doctor, please get to work.

00:09:28.580 --> 00:09:29.590
Yeah, yeah.

00:09:35.640 --> 00:09:37.080
So spicy!

00:09:40.450 --> 00:09:41.520
It was obvious.

00:09:41.520 --> 00:09:43.930
Kuro, why aren't you freaking out?

00:09:46.020 --> 00:09:47.680
Why do you look so smug?

00:09:47.680 --> 00:09:49.920
Is that one not spicy at all?

00:09:53.970 --> 00:09:55.610
You're being uncouth!

00:09:56.710 --> 00:10:02.200
Pot stickers can conceal spiciness 
by enveloping it inside their skins.

00:10:02.620 --> 00:10:08.200
She's unconsciously wrapping painful words she 
doesn't want to hear inside those pot stickers.

00:10:08.570 --> 00:10:11.710
Here, Yuu. Are you okay with hot drinks?

00:10:11.710 --> 00:10:13.750
Yuu, are you okay?!

00:10:13.750 --> 00:10:15.100
Did you get any on you?!

00:10:15.340 --> 00:10:18.750
Excuse me, but who are you talking to?

00:10:22.880 --> 00:10:24.840
Last October...

00:10:25.230 --> 00:10:27.820
It must be that grade school boy.

00:10:26.310 --> 00:10:27.810
<b>Please Wait</b>

00:10:28.150 --> 00:10:29.950
Oh, was that it?

00:10:29.950 --> 00:10:35.050
Since it was on my route to school,
 I remember the crowd of reporters.

00:10:33.070 --> 00:10:35.070
<b>- Kidnapping cases on the rise 
- Japanese kidnapping and murder cases - Wikepedoa
- Incarcerated kidnapper tells all: behind the kidnapping—shocking revelations 
- Grade school student murder—neighbors witnessed suspicious man 
- Suspicious person spotted—police urge residents with small children to exercise caution 
- Pitfall going to and from school—where did the student go? 
- Heart-rending voices of the parents—parents speak to kidnapper through media</b>

00:10:36.530 --> 00:10:37.420
Found it.

00:10:38.600 --> 00:10:41.320
Yuu, I'm turning off the lights.

00:10:46.610 --> 00:10:49.450
<i>I have to cure her. After all...</i>

00:10:50.520 --> 00:10:53.330
Come on. Share, you two.

00:10:53.330 --> 00:10:54.520
Aw, man.

00:10:54.520 --> 00:10:57.470
If I didn't have a brother, 
it would be all mine.

00:10:58.170 --> 00:11:01.790
<i>If I didn't have a brother, 
it would be all mine.</i>

00:11:13.550 --> 00:11:15.760
<i>It's all my fault</i>

00:11:16.980 --> 00:11:22.950
<b>Grade School Boy Kidnapping and Murder Case</b>

00:11:17.950 --> 00:11:19.690
<i>that he's gone.</i>

00:11:25.260 --> 00:11:26.960
Mom, did you know?

00:11:26.960 --> 00:11:33.210
Tomatoes have sticky stems that trap bugs 
that they consume for nutrients, and—

00:11:33.210 --> 00:11:35.630
I wanted more of that pork bun!

00:11:35.630 --> 00:11:37.090
Don't be so selfish!

00:11:37.090 --> 00:11:38.880
We always have to share, though!

00:11:38.880 --> 00:11:40.220
You should buy us each our own!

00:11:40.220 --> 00:11:42.550
Then you wouldn't be able to eat dinner.

00:11:42.550 --> 00:11:44.470
I don't like you or Yuu anymore.

00:11:47.210 --> 00:11:49.260
You burned yourself.

00:11:49.590 --> 00:11:51.900
Are you okay? Does it hurt?

00:11:51.900 --> 00:11:53.520
I'm fine.

00:11:53.520 --> 00:11:56.260
I'll make Rio apologize later.

00:12:00.530 --> 00:12:01.890
Hey, Mom—

00:12:01.890 --> 00:12:05.370
I'm sorry, Yuu. I'm going to check on Rio.

00:12:08.330 --> 00:12:11.780
Don't cry. I know it wasn't on purpose.

00:12:19.760 --> 00:12:22.380
<b>Thank You For 7 Years</b>

00:12:19.760 --> 00:12:22.380
100 yen Rice Ball Fair!

00:12:19.760 --> 00:12:22.380
<b>Cigarettes</b>

00:12:19.760 --> 00:12:22.380
<b>Alcohol</b>

00:12:27.370 --> 00:12:30.000
<i>I hope this cheers Rio up.</i>

00:12:38.700 --> 00:12:43.940
Hey, kid. Could you give me some directions?

00:13:03.070 --> 00:13:05.000
Yuu... Yuu...

00:13:06.040 --> 00:13:10.260
It's my fault that he hasn't 
come home in a week.

00:13:10.870 --> 00:13:14.470
It looked like he wanted 
to say something back then.

00:13:14.840 --> 00:13:18.400
It's my fault for paying attention 
to Rio instead of listening to him.

00:13:19.600 --> 00:13:20.910
To Rio...

00:13:22.710 --> 00:13:24.970
We received eyewitness 
information regarding Yuu-kun!

00:13:25.780 --> 00:13:30.140
On the day he went missing, he bought 
pork buns at a nearby convenience store.

00:14:09.130 --> 00:14:09.820
What's wrong?!

00:14:11.040 --> 00:14:13.180
Yuu... Yuu...

00:14:14.410 --> 00:14:17.820
Yuu's arm...

00:14:24.330 --> 00:14:26.200
Tell us about the case.

00:14:24.790 --> 00:14:26.860
Is there any reason someone 
would resent you?

00:14:25.560 --> 00:14:27.330
What was Yuu-kun like?

00:14:28.900 --> 00:14:33.090
<i>In the case of missing boy Miyata Yuu-kun, 
the results of the DNA test have shown...</i>

00:14:35.130 --> 00:14:36.370
Mom—

00:14:35.570 --> 00:14:36.850
No.

00:14:37.700 --> 00:14:39.570
Yuu isn't dead.

00:14:40.660 --> 00:14:43.140
Stop. Please stop.

00:14:43.470 --> 00:14:45.970
Stop. No, no, no.

00:14:45.970 --> 00:14:47.840
Please stop. No, please.

00:14:47.840 --> 00:14:49.730
No, no, no, no, no...

00:14:50.330 --> 00:14:52.860
I don't want to hear it anymore.

00:15:01.280 --> 00:15:04.350
Ma'am, are you all right?

00:15:04.350 --> 00:15:07.220
I'm sure things are hard 
since Yuu-kun is gone.

00:15:07.900 --> 00:15:09.120
Yuu?

00:15:10.150 --> 00:15:13.990
Yuu's right here.

00:15:18.810 --> 00:15:20.630
True hallucinations?

00:15:20.940 --> 00:15:26.690
Right. She's hallucinating that something 
that doesn't exist is with her.

00:15:27.320 --> 00:15:33.640
She's hallucinating her child in order to 
protect herself from a painful reality.

00:15:33.950 --> 00:15:36.940
That's what the psychiatrist said.

00:15:36.940 --> 00:15:38.240
I see.

00:15:38.240 --> 00:15:42.310
You suggested we see how things go for once 
because you received that information.

00:15:42.310 --> 00:15:43.260
Yeah.

00:15:44.710 --> 00:15:46.650
The Pearl of Night Voices.

00:15:47.870 --> 00:15:54.340
You said you'd cure your mom, so 
naturally, you'll pay the price.

00:15:54.340 --> 00:15:56.980
Whether or not she's cured is up to you.

00:16:08.610 --> 00:16:10.750
Put that up to your ear.

00:16:11.570 --> 00:16:14.290
Hello, hello. Do you copy?

00:16:15.320 --> 00:16:19.860
When you speak into it, your voice 
can be heard in the other shell.

00:16:20.290 --> 00:16:22.050
Like a phone?

00:16:22.050 --> 00:16:24.250
But I don't hear anything.

00:16:24.250 --> 00:16:29.620
Normally, they can only be used by 
a man and woman who are in love.

00:16:30.290 --> 00:16:34.260
They were used long ago by such a couple.

00:16:34.870 --> 00:16:40.110
With these, they could hear each other's 
voices even when they were apart.

00:16:40.840 --> 00:16:46.260
But the more you speak, the more your 
voices are stolen by the shells,

00:16:46.260 --> 00:16:48.280
eventually disappearing entirely.

00:16:48.280 --> 00:16:52.430
If you and your partner exchange the pearls 
you nurtured with your voices and eat them,

00:16:52.430 --> 00:16:55.230
your love will last forever.

00:16:55.230 --> 00:16:57.480
It's like a magic charm.

00:16:57.950 --> 00:16:59.820
Sounds like a fairy tale.

00:17:00.890 --> 00:17:01.860
You're right.

00:17:01.860 --> 00:17:05.470
Anyway, a mother and her son are a 
man and woman who love each other.

00:17:05.470 --> 00:17:08.510
You and your mom should hold on to those.

00:17:10.770 --> 00:17:12.380
Do you understand?

00:17:12.380 --> 00:17:18.020
As you speak to your mom through 
this, your voice will disappear.

00:17:18.860 --> 00:17:22.640
Once she learns her son's voice is 
disappearing, she'll try to hear it,

00:17:22.640 --> 00:17:26.520
even if it means accepting the painful 
reality she wrapped up in those pot stickers.

00:17:26.850 --> 00:17:31.580
In other words, this treatment 
method weighs you against that.

00:17:33.520 --> 00:17:36.020
Will that mysterious item cure her?

00:17:36.020 --> 00:17:38.030
I have a plan.

00:17:38.280 --> 00:17:43.050
It's possible that just putting him 
on the scale won't change anything,

00:17:43.050 --> 00:17:45.800
so I'm going to tip it for them.

00:17:54.800 --> 00:18:00.300
Welcome <b>to Yuzuru!!</b>

00:17:55.650 --> 00:17:58.420
Onii-chan, where are you?

00:17:58.420 --> 00:18:00.300
Huh? Rio-kun?

00:18:03.090 --> 00:18:07.600
Good timing. I was just on 
my way to interview you.

00:18:07.600 --> 00:18:10.010
I already told you to stop showing up!

00:18:10.010 --> 00:18:12.100
Don't be like that.

00:18:12.420 --> 00:18:15.810
Sometimes people come forward with 
information after reading an article.

00:18:17.660 --> 00:18:21.270
Don't you want the culprit who killed 
your brother to be arrested?

00:18:24.190 --> 00:18:26.190
Don't assume my brother is dead!

00:18:53.530 --> 00:18:55.270
Rio.

00:18:55.270 --> 00:18:59.210
That's the laundry. Why is it wet?

00:19:01.160 --> 00:19:02.310
It's raining?

00:19:03.740 --> 00:19:07.550
Why didn't I notice?

00:19:08.540 --> 00:19:10.960
The rain is awfully quiet.

00:19:18.010 --> 00:19:20.550
Hey, there was just enough.

00:19:22.070 --> 00:19:24.900
How unusual for you not to 
drink out of the carton.

00:19:24.900 --> 00:19:26.380
It's a little cold today.

00:19:26.380 --> 00:19:28.310
I'm making hot milk.

00:19:28.820 --> 00:19:32.050
Doctor, I'm leaving for the day.

00:19:32.050 --> 00:19:35.740
All right. You've got something 
to do at home, right?

00:19:35.740 --> 00:19:36.560
Yes.

00:19:36.860 --> 00:19:37.570
Doctor!

00:19:40.870 --> 00:19:41.820
Rio.

00:19:42.240 --> 00:19:45.680
What should I do? My mom's ears...

00:19:46.450 --> 00:19:48.290
Hurry, come quickly!

00:19:48.290 --> 00:19:51.260
Okay, okay. Hold on while I lock up.

00:19:51.500 --> 00:19:53.840
You don't need to turn off the lights?

00:19:53.840 --> 00:19:55.970
Oh, it's fine.

00:19:55.970 --> 00:19:59.160
I'll come right back as soon 
as I've checked on his mom.

00:20:00.500 --> 00:20:02.220
Hurry, hurry!

00:20:02.220 --> 00:20:04.270
Calm down.

00:20:04.500 --> 00:20:05.910
Be careful.

00:20:10.340 --> 00:20:13.440
Don't run. You'll slip.

00:20:23.560 --> 00:20:25.440
Hey, where are you going?!

00:20:25.440 --> 00:20:27.150
Your house isn't back there!

00:20:27.150 --> 00:20:28.780
I saw something move.

00:20:28.780 --> 00:20:29.990
It could be my brother.

00:20:29.990 --> 00:20:32.080
What? Calm down, you idiot!

00:20:32.080 --> 00:20:33.580
Your brother is...

00:20:36.670 --> 00:20:38.120
Aw, jeez!

00:20:41.970 --> 00:20:45.760
<b>Do Not Enter</b>

00:21:24.490 --> 00:21:25.870
I'm home.

00:21:29.040 --> 00:21:30.190
What's wrong?

00:21:32.150 --> 00:21:33.420
Rio...

00:21:36.470 --> 00:21:38.460
He's not back yet.

00:21:46.990 --> 00:21:47.940
Doctor!

00:21:49.940 --> 00:21:51.310
Doctor!

00:21:53.060 --> 00:21:54.600
Doctor!

00:23:25.930 --> 00:23:26.890
<i>Doctor!</i>

